  "body": {
    "givenName": "iFly",
    "image": {
      "@type": "ImageObject",
      "contentUrl": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/026iFly/swada/main/assets/iFly.png"
    },
    "motivations": "I run as a DRep because Cardano's on-chain governance is one of the more serious attempts I've seen to translate decentralization from a slogan into a working institution — and institutions like that only succeed when enough people with real-world skin in the game show up to maintain them.\n\nMy own perspective is built from three disciplines that all happen to share one rule: complex systems work only if you trust the data, the procedures, and the people who maintain them. I've been a commercial pilot for ten years (currently flying for Norwegian, also a flight instructor), so I think a lot about safety culture, redundancy, and how small unchecked drift becomes a big problem later. I'm a co-founder of Intellishares SA, where we use Cardano to tokenize green-energy assets — solar systems, batteries, inverters — so I deploy blockchain in the regulated, physical world every week, not just argue about it on social media. And I serve on several volunteer boards (AOPA Sweden, the Gävle Sjöscouter scout organization, our local flight club), which has taught me what consensus-building actually feels like when there's no fork to take.\n\nCardano governance affects how the broader world adopts decentralized technology. I want to help that process succeed — pragmatically, transparently, and with a long-time-horizon mindset.",
    "objectives": "My priorities as a DRep:\n\n* **Real-world utility first.** I vote for proposals that move Cardano toward concrete adoption — tokenized real-world assets, programmable settlement, identity that ordinary people can use without a cryptography PhD, and infrastructure for green-energy investment. Less abstraction, more shipped.\n* **Validator decentralization.** A healthy long tail of small, independent stake pools (SWADA among them) is what makes the network resilient. I oppose proposals that incidentally concentrate stake, and I support those that protect minority operators.\n* **Sustainability — environmental and economic.** Cardano's energy footprint is already an advantage; I want governance decisions that compound it through verifiable, blockchain-anchored climate work.\n* **Transparent reasoning.** Where time and confidentiality allow, I'll publish a short written rationale alongside every meaningful vote — so delegators can see *why*, not just *how*, and disagree with me intelligently if they want to.\n* **Cross-disciplinary evaluation.** I evaluate each proposal through more than one frame — aviation safety thinking (what's the failure mode?), energy-engineering pragmatism (does this actually work at scale?), and product/business sense (does anyone use this?). One-axis reasoning is how bad decisions get made.",
    "qualifications": "Ten years as a commercial pilot, currently a line and instructor pilot with Norwegian Air Sweden. Aviation has trained me in continuous risk assessment, procedural discipline, and operating in environments where casual decisions have permanent consequences — directly applicable to governance work where small parameter changes ripple through every protocol layer.\n\nCo-founder and active operator at Intellishares SA, a Cardano-based green-energy tokenization project. I've personally designed and installed solar systems, tested inverters and batteries, prototyped electronic circuit boards and custom enclosures, and integrated all of it with on-chain settlement. I evaluate proposals from the perspective of someone who actually deploys this technology in regulated, physical-world contexts.\n\nBoard-level service in three Swedish organizations: AOPA Sweden (aircraft owner & pilot advocacy), Gävle Sjöscouter (Sea Scouts — Vice President), and our local flight club (Chair). Each has taught me to balance competing member interests, build consensus across disagreement, and be accountable to a membership over multi-year horizons — habits that translate directly to DRep work.\n\nLanguages: Swedish, English (both fluent), Italian (learning). I read governance proposals carefully and engage substantively before voting. And I run the SWADA Cardano stake pool — my own ADA is pledged into the network whose governance I help shape.",
    "paymentAddress": "addr1q856gtlurau0wnrz8nzap22cww32wa77p5mu3vdpywgcshl64zph7c4yajs044l004zhdmutkdgnutqkj3q79my7y9vs948aw5",
